---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Showcase — HarvTech"
  description="Working portfolio pieces — this site, a reference Azure landing zone, the data platform, and more."
>
  <section class="container-page py-20">
    <p class="eyebrow mb-4">Showcase</p>
    <h1 class="title-display mb-6 hero-gradient max-w-3xl leading-tight">
      Working portfolio.
    </h1>
    <p class="body-muted mb-12 max-w-2xl text-lg">
      Public projects, with the source on GitHub and the trade-offs
      written up in plain English. Detailed case studies dropping in
      one by one.
    </p>

    <div class="grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="card p-7">
        <span class="badge-accent mb-3 inline-block">Live</span>
        <p class="title-card mt-3 mb-2">harvtech.co.uk infrastructure</p>
        <p class="body-muted mb-4 text-sm">
          This site. Astro + Tailwind output, served from Azure Storage
          $web, behind Front Door with WAF. Terraform across two stacks
          with OIDC-federated CI/CD. The git history is intentionally
          honest about what worked first time and what didn't.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/HarvtechUK/harvtech-site"
          rel="noopener"
          target="_blank"
          class="btn-secondary text-sm"
        >
          View the repo
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="card p-7">
        <span class="badge-accent mb-3 inline-block">Live</span>
        <p class="title-card mt-3 mb-2">Azure data platform</p>
        <p class="body-muted mb-4 text-sm">
          ADLS Gen2 lakehouse (medallion raw/cleansed/curated), Cosmos
          DB on the free tier, Data Factory orchestrator stub, and a
          Databricks workspace. Stays under £1/month by deploying the
          resources without running the workloads — the IaC pattern is
          the showcase, drawn from prior real-world experience.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          <a
            href="/docs/architecture/data-platform-hld"
            class="btn-secondary text-sm"
          >
            Read the HLD
          </a>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/HarvtechUK/harvtech-site/tree/main/data-platform"
            rel="noopener"
            target="_blank"
            class="btn-secondary text-sm"
          >
            View the Terraform
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card p-7">
        <p class="eyebrow mb-3">In progress</p>
        <p class="title-card mb-2">Reference Azure landing zone</p>
        <p class="body-muted text-sm">
          A well-architected landing zone in Terraform &mdash; hub-spoke
          networking, private endpoints, Entra Conditional Access,
          Defender for Cloud, image scanning, and WAF at the edge. AI
          (Azure OpenAI / Foundry) drops in as one demonstrated workload
          on top, alongside data and app-tier examples. Coming as a
          separate repo with this site as its case-study home.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
